[30.929, "[39m.\u001b[21G\u001b[22mThe compiler's default fused multiply-add is \u001b[67Gn, and\u001b[74Gthat isn'\u001b[84G fast-math.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mLimitations\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GResults\u001b[13Garen't\u001b[20Gbit-identical\u001b[34Gto\u001b[37Gthe\u001b[41Greference,\u001b[52Gbecause\u001b[60Gsums\u001b[65Gare\u001b[69Gadded\u001b[75Gin\u001b[78Ga\u001b[80Gdifferent\u001b[90Gorder\u001b[96Gand\u001b[100Gthe\u001b[104Gmath\u001b[109Gfunctions\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  are my own.\u001b[17GAll\u001b[21Gtop\u001b[25Gtokens\u001b[32Gmatched\u001b[40Gin\u001b[43Gtesting,\u001b[52Gbut\u001b[56Ga\u001b[58Gnear-tie\u001b[67Gin\u001b[70Glogits\u001b[77Gcould\u001b[83Gin\u001b[86Gprinciple\u001b[96Gpick\u001b[101Ga\u001b[103Gdifferent\u001b[113Gtoken.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BThe code is ARM-only: i\u001b[29G uses NEON and won't build on x86.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GSome inputs\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Ginterface doesn't defin\u001b[45G (u\u001b[49Gknown commands, out-of-range ids,\u001b[83Gsequences \u001b[94Gonger than 1024, a\u001b[113Gdecoded\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gzero byte) are ha\u001b[23Gdled defen\u001b[34Gively\u001b[40Gbut\u001b[45Gith behaviour\u001b[59GI chose\u001b[67Gmyself.\u001b[75GNOTES.md\u001b[84Glists\u001b[90Geach\u001b[95Gone.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcheck.py\u001b[39m passing is necessary bu\u001b[39Gnot sufficient;\u001b[55Gthe final\u001b"]
